--------------------------- MODULE AsymmetricQuorums ---------------------------
\* Asymmetric quorum systems (Cachin et al.; "Symmetry All the Way Down",
\* DISC 2026) and their embedding as condensed learner graphs.  Definitions
\* only; the lemmas and theorems live in their own modules (AQ*, Asymmetric*).
\*
\* An asymmetric fail-prone system fps gives every acceptor i its own family
\* fps[i] of fail-prone sets: i assumes the actual faulty set is contained in
\* SOME member of fps[i].  Canonical quorums are the complements.  The
\* embedding takes learners = acceptors, each learner's quorums generated by
\* the complements of its own fail-prone sets, and the safety sets of an edge
\* generated by the complements of the COMMONLY foreseen faulty sets (the
\* subset-closure intersection F_i^* \cap F_j^*, here AQCommon).  The
\* interface's SafetySets/Quorums operators close generators upward, matching
\* the star-closure on the fail-prone side.
EXTENDS LearnerGraphInterface

\* Typing: every acceptor gets a family of potential faulty sets.
AQTypeOK(fps) == fps \in [Acceptors -> SUBSET SUBSET Acceptors]

\* Nontriviality: everyone has at least one failure assumption.
AQNonTrivial(fps) == \A i \in Acceptors : fps[i] # {}

\* i's assumptions foresee the faulty set `faulty' (i is WISE when `faulty'
\* is the actual faulty set): faulty \in fps[i]^*.
AQWise(fps, i, faulty) == \E f \in fps[i] : faulty \subseteq f

\* Every member of the edge e foresees `faulty' (JOINTLY wise).
AQJointlyWise(fps, e, faulty) == \A i \in e : AQWise(fps, i, faulty)

\* The commonly foreseen faulty sets of edge e: the subset-closed
\* intersection of the members' starred fail-prone systems.
AQCommon(fps, e) == {f \in SUBSET Acceptors : AQJointlyWise(fps, e, f)}

\* The B^3 condition ("Symmetry All the Way Down", Definition 3.2): no two
\* fail-prone sets of two acceptors, together with a commonly foreseen faulty
\* set, cover all acceptors.
AQB3(fps) ==
  \A i \in Acceptors : \A j \in Acceptors :
  \A fi \in fps[i] : \A fj \in fps[j] :
  \A fij \in AQCommon(fps, {i, j}) :
    \E a \in Acceptors : a \notin fi /\ a \notin fj /\ a \notin fij

\* The ambient learner graph IS the embedding of fps: learners are the
\* acceptors; quorum generators are the canonical quorums (complements of
\* fps[i]); safety-set generators of edge e are the complements of the
\* commonly foreseen faulty sets.
AQEmbedded(fps) ==
  /\ Learners = Acceptors
  /\ SpecifiedQuorums = [i \in Acceptors |-> {Acceptors \ f : f \in fps[i]}]
  /\ SpecifiedSafetySets =
       [e \in LearnerPairs |-> {Acceptors \ f : f \in AQCommon(fps, e)}]
====================================================================
